# Keep PII and bulk out of the build context.
# Anything listed here CANNOT end up baked into an image layer.

# --- PII / identity (NEVER into an image) ---
.env
profile.local.json
profile.*.local.json
*.local.json
data/state.sqlite
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
logs/
results/
serpwatch-hits/
removals/
*.removal.json
snapshots/
needs-fix/
heartbeat.json
health-report.txt
run-log.jsonl
escalations/
letters/
complaints/
audit-log.jsonl
escalation-rules.json
data/brokers.json

# --- vendored Go source: needed by the eraser-builder stage only ---
# The FINAL image never contains this source, only the compiled binary
# (multi-stage build in Dockerfile) -- but the docker build CONTEXT does
# need it now, so unlike before this is no longer excluded wholesale.
# vendor/eraser/ (~1.7MB) is small enough that no further trimming here is
# worth the complexity of a nested negation pattern.

# --- dev / VCS / build noise ---
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
tests/
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
.preflight-state.json
*.md
!README.md
